<article class="env-proposition" id="7D37B6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/7D37B6">Proposition <span data-tag="7D37B6">5.2.4.4</span>.</a> Let $\calM $ be a fibrant simplicial category equipped with a functor $p: \calM \rightarrow \Delta ^1$ (here we identify $\Delta ^1$ with the two-object category whose nerve is $\Delta ^1$), so that we may view $\calM $ as a correspondence between the simplicial categories $\calC = p^{-1} \{ 0\} $ and $\calD = p^{-1} \{ 1\} $. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The map $p$ is a Cartesian fibration. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
For every object $D \in \calD $, there exists a morphism $f: C \rightarrow D$ in $\calM $ which induces homotopy equivalences 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{\calC }(C',C) \rightarrow \bHom _{\calM }(C',D) \]
</div>
<p>
 for every $C' \in \calC $. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from Proposition <a href="/tag/FADC3B" data-tag="FADC3B">2.4.1.10</a>, since nonempty morphism spaces in $\Delta ^1$ are contractible. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>